-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1: Subchapter V (stock and dividends), sections 151 to 153, 155 to 158 and 161.
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. It takes nobody's point of view; the seat layer is dg3-seat.l4.
--
-- The source is the plain-text rendering de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt of the Delaware Code Online (through 85 Del. Laws, c. 550),
-- made by a converter script. It is not the official text. `-- src:N | ...` is a slice of line N of that file; an ellipsis means the line goes on.
--
-- Conventions used throughout this piece:
--   * A rule is a BOOLEAN decision named as a proposition, with its section locator first. A figure is a noun phrase.
--   * "Unless otherwise provided in the certificate": the displacing provision is a separate input; the Law's default stands when it is absent.
--   * A judgment the text hands to someone else ("a reasonable time", "as soon as practicable") is a plain input, never decided here.
--   * A case the text does not answer is NOTHING in a MAYBE, never FALSE.
--   * Sections 151 to 158 and 161 are among those that section 114(b)(2) takes out of the stockholder-to-member reading of section 114(a),
--     so no member reading is encoded in this module (section 114 is encoded by dg1).
--   * Out of range: section 103 (dg1), section 156 and 202 (in this piece but taken as stated facts where the text only cites them), 218(a) (dg4),
--     section 245 (dg5), section 364 (dg10), the Investment Company Act of 1940 (15 U.S.C., not an input).

§ `Section 151: classes and series of stock; redemption; rights`

-- Where the terms of a class or series (or its redemption, preferences or conversion) are stated, as section 151(a) lets them be stated:
-- in the certificate of incorporation or an amendment, or in a resolution of the board adopted under authority expressly vested in it by the certificate.
-- The text names only those two places. A term stated in the bylaws or nowhere is therefore not one this subsection authorises (Fork F1).
-- src:468 | Every corporation may issue 1 or more classes of stock or 1 or more series of stock within any class thereof, any or all of which classes may be of stock with par value or stock without par value and which classes or series may have such voting powers, full or limited, or no voting powers, and such designations, preferences and relative, participating, optional or other special rights, and qualifications, limitations or restrictions thereof, as shall be stated and expressed in the certificate of incorporation or of any amendment thereto, or in the resolution or resolutions providing for the issue of such stock adopted by the board of directors pursuant to authority expressly vested in it by the provisions of its certificate of incorporation …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 151(a) (src:468)
GIVEN `where the terms are stated` IS A `Where a provision is made`
      `the certificate of incorporation expressly vests the authority in the board of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 151(a) the terms are stated where that subsection allows` `where the terms are stated` `the certificate of incorporation expressly vests the authority in the board of directors` MEANS
    CONSIDER `where the terms are stated`
    WHEN `in the certificate of incorporation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `in a resolution of the board of directors` THEN `the certificate of incorporation expressly vests the authority in the board of directors`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The nouns of section 151(a): how the terms of one class or series are fixed.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 151(a) (src:468)
DECLARE `s 151(a) Terms of a class or series` HAS
    `where the terms are stated`                                                 IS A `Where a provision is made`
    `authority to fix the terms is expressly vested in the board by the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a term depends on facts ascertainable outside the instrument that states it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the instrument clearly and expressly sets forth how those facts operate on the term` IS A BOOLEAN

-- A class or series may have the voting powers, designations, preferences, rights and qualifications that are stated as above;
-- any of them may be made dependent on facts ascertainable outside the instrument, provided the manner in which the facts operate is clearly and expressly set forth.
-- src:468 | Every corporation may issue 1 or more classes of stock or 1 or more series of stock within any class thereof, any or all of which classes may be of stock with par value or stock without par value and which classes or series may have such voting powers, full or limited, or no voting powers, and such designations, preferences and relative, participating, optional or other special rights, and qualifications, limitations or restrictions thereof, as shall be stated and expressed in the certificate of incorporation or of any amendment thereto, or in the resolution or resolutions providing for the issue of such stock adopted by the board of directors pursuant to authority expressly vested in it by the provisions of its certificate of incorporation …
-- src:468 | Any of the voting powers, designations, preferences, rights and qualifications, limitations or restrictions of any such class or series of stock may be made dependent upon facts ascertainable outside the certificate of incorporation or of any amendment thereto, or outside the resolution or resolutions providing for the issue of such stock adopted by the board of directors pursuant to authority expressly vested in it by its certificate of incorporation, provided that the manner in which such facts shall operate upon the voting powers, designations, preferences, rights and qualifications, limitations or restrictions of such class or series of stock is clearly and expressly set forth in the certificate of incorporation or in the resolution or resolutions providing for the issue of such stock adopted by the board of directors …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 151(a) (src:468)
GIVEN t IS A `s 151(a) Terms of a class or series`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 151(a) the terms of the class or series are authorised` t MEANS
        `s 151(a) the terms are stated where that subsection allows` (t's `where the terms are stated`) (t's `authority to fix the terms is expressly vested in the board by the certificate`)
    AND (    (NOT t's `a term depends on facts ascertainable outside the instrument that states it`)
         OR  t's `the instrument clearly and expressly sets forth how those facts operate on the term`)

-- "The term 'facts,' as used in this subsection, includes, but is not limited to, the occurrence of any event, including a determination or action by any person or body, including the corporation."
-- An inclusive definition: the occurrence of an event is a fact; whether anything else is one the text does not say, so that case is NOTHING.
-- src:468 | The term “facts,” as used in this subsection, includes, but is not limited to, the occurrence of any event, including a determination or action by any person or body, including the corporation …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 151(a) (src:468)
GIVEN `the matter is the occurrence of an event, including a determination or action by any person or body (the corporation included)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 151(a) the matter is a fact for the purposes of that subsection` `the matter is the occurrence of an event, including a determination or action by any person or body (the corporation included)` MEANS
    IF `the matter is the occurrence of an event, including a determination or action by any person or body (the corporation included)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- "The power to increase or decrease or otherwise adjust the capital stock as provided in this chapter shall apply to all or any such classes of stock."
-- src:468 | The power to increase or decrease or otherwise adjust the capital stock as provided in this chapter shall apply to all or any such classes of stock.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 151(a) (src:468)
GIVEN `the stock is of a class or series that the corporation may issue under section 151(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 151(a) the power to adjust the capital stock applies to the class or series` `the stock is of a class or series that the corporation may issue under section 151(a)` MEANS
    `the stock is of a class or series that the corporation may issue under section 151(a)`

-- Redemption (section 151(b)). The three ways a redemption can be triggered.
-- src:469 | Any stock of any class or series may be made subject to redemption by the corporation at its option or at the option of the holders of such stock or upon the happening of a specified event …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 151(b) (src:469)
DECLARE `s 151(b) How a redemption is triggered` IS ONE OF
    `at the option of the corporation under s 151(b)`
    `at the option of the holders of the stock under s 151(b)`
    `upon the happening of a specified event under s 151(b)`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 151(b) (src:469-471)
DECLARE `s 151(b) Redemption terms` HAS
    `how the redemption is triggered`                                                                              IS A `s 151(b) How a redemption is triggered`
    `immediately following the redemption 1 or more shares of 1 or more classes or series with full voting powers will be outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- out of range: the Investment Company Act of 1940 (15 U.S.C. § 80a-1 et seq.), not among the inputs
    `the stock is stock of a regulated investment company registered under the Investment Company Act of 1940`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the corporation holds a licence or franchise from a governmental agency to conduct its business, or is a member of a national securities exchange, conditioned on holders of its stock possessing prescribed qualifications` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the redemption is to the extent necessary to prevent the loss of the licence, franchise or membership or to reinstate it` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Stock may be made redeemable, but immediately afterwards the corporation must have outstanding shares with full voting powers.
-- Notwithstanding that: (1) stock of a registered investment company may be made redeemable at the option of the corporation or of the holders;
-- (2) stock of a corporation whose licence, franchise or exchange membership is conditioned on its holders' qualifications may be made redeemable to the extent necessary.
-- src:469 | Any stock of any class or series may be made subject to redemption by the corporation at its option or at the option of the holders of such stock or upon the happening of a specified event; provided however, that immediately following any such redemption the corporation shall have outstanding 1 or more shares of 1 or more classes or series of stock, which share, or shares together, shall have full voting powers …
-- src:470 | Any stock of a regulated investment company registered under the Investment Company Act of 1940 [15 U.S.C. § 80 a-1 et seq.], as heretofore or hereafter amended, may be made subject to redemption by the corporation at its option or at the option of the holders of such stock.
-- src:471 | Any stock of a corporation which holds (directly or indirectly) a license or franchise from a governmental agency to conduct its business or is a member of a national securities exchange, which license, franchise or membership is conditioned upon some or all of the holders of its stock possessing prescribed qualifications, may be made subject to redemption by the corporation to the extent necessary to prevent the loss of such license, franchise or membership or to reinstate it.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 151(b) (src:469-471)
GIVEN r IS A `s 151(b) Redemption terms`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 151(b) the stock may be made subject to redemption` r MEANS
        r's `immediately following the redemption 1 or more shares of 1 or more classes or series with full voting powers will be outstanding`
    OR (    r's `the stock is stock of a regulated investment company registered under the Investment Company Act of 1940`
        AND (    r's `how the redemption is triggered` EQUALS `at the option of the corporation under s 151(b)`
             OR  r's `how the redemption is triggered` EQUALS `at the option of the holders of the stock under s 151(b)`))
    OR (    r's `the corporation holds a licence or franchise from a governmental agency to conduct its business, or is a member of a national securities exchange, conditioned on holders of its stock possessing prescribed qualifications`
        AND r's `the redemption is to the extent necessary to prevent the loss of the licence, franchise or membership or to reinstate it`)

-- Redeemable stock may be redeemed for cash, property or rights (including securities of the same or another corporation), at the times, prices, rates and adjustments
-- stated in the certificate or in a board resolution adopted under section 151(a). The kinds of consideration are listed without limit, so the test is where the terms are stated.
-- src:472 | Any stock which may be made redeemable under this section may be redeemed for cash, property or rights, including securities of the same or another corporation, at such time or times, price or prices, or rate or rates, and with such adjustments, as shall be stated in the certificate of incorporation or in the resolution or resolutions providing for the issue of such stock adopted by the board of directors pursuant to subsection (a) of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 151(b) (src:472)
GIVEN `where the redemption terms are stated` IS A `Where a provision is made`
      `the certificate of incorporation expressly vests the authority in the board of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 151(b) the redemption price and times are stated where that subsection requires` `where the redemption terms are stated` `the certificate of incorporation expressly vests the authority in the board of directors` MEANS
    `s 151(a) the terms are stated where that subsection allows` `where the redemption terms are stated` `the certificate of incorporation expressly vests the authority in the board of directors`

-- Section 151(c): preferred or special stock carries a right to dividends as stated, in preference to or in relation to other stock, cumulative or noncumulative as stated.
-- src:473 | The holders of preferred or special stock of any class or of any series thereof shall be entitled to receive dividends at such rates, on such conditions and at such times as shall be stated in the certificate of incorporation or in the resolution or resolutions providing for the issue of such stock adopted by the board of directors as hereinabove provided, payable in preference to, or in such relation to, the dividends payable on any other class or classes or of any other series of stock, and cumulative or noncumulative as shall be so stated and expressed. When dividends upon the preferred and special stocks, if any, to the extent of the preference to which such stocks are entitled, shall have been paid or declared and set apart for payment, a dividend on the remaining class or classes or series of stock may then be paid out of the remaining assets of the corporation available for dividends as elsewhere in this chapter provided.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 151(c) (src:473)
GIVEN `the stock is preferred or special stock of a class or series` IS A BOOLEAN
      `where the dividend terms are stated` IS A `Where a provision is made`
      `the certificate of incorporation expressly vests the authority in the board of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 151(c) the holder of the preferred or special stock is entitled to dividends as stated` `the stock is preferred or special stock of a class or series` `where the dividend terms are stated` `the certificate of incorporation expressly vests the authority in the board of directors` MEANS
        `the stock is preferred or special stock of a class or series`
    AND `s 151(a) the terms are stated where that subsection allows` `where the dividend terms are stated` `the certificate of incorporation expressly vests the authority in the board of directors`

-- Once the preferred and special stocks' dividends, to the extent of their preference, have been paid or declared and set apart for payment,
-- a dividend on the remaining classes or series may then be paid out of the remaining assets available for dividends as elsewhere in the chapter provided.
-- src:473 | When dividends upon the preferred and special stocks, if any, to the extent of the preference to which such stocks are entitled, shall have been paid or declared and set apart for payment, a dividend on the remaining class or classes or series of stock may then be paid out of the remaining assets of the corporation available for dividends as elsewhere in this chapter provided.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 151(c) (src:473)
GIVEN `the dividends on the preferred and special stocks, to the extent of their preference, have been paid or declared and set apart for payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      -- out of range: the chapter's other limits on dividends (section 170 is in the sibling module dg3-capital-dividends; this input is its outcome)
      `the remaining assets are available for dividends as elsewhere in the chapter provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 151(c) a dividend on the remaining classes or series may then be paid` `the dividends on the preferred and special stocks, to the extent of their preference, have been paid or declared and set apart for payment` `the remaining assets are available for dividends as elsewhere in the chapter provided` MEANS
        `the dividends on the preferred and special stocks, to the extent of their preference, have been paid or declared and set apart for payment`
    AND `the remaining assets are available for dividends as elsewhere in the chapter provided`

-- Section 151(d): preferred or special stock carries the rights on dissolution or on a distribution of assets that are stated.
-- src:474 | The holders of the preferred or special stock of any class or of any series thereof shall be entitled to such rights upon the dissolution of, or upon any distribution of the assets of, the corporation as shall be stated in the certificate of incorporation or in the resolution or resolutions providing for the issue of such stock adopted by the board of directors as hereinabove provided.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 151(d) (src:474)
GIVEN `the stock is preferred or special stock of a class or series` IS A BOOLEAN
      `where the rights on dissolution or distribution are stated` IS A `Where a provision is made`
      `the certificate of incorporation expressly vests the authority in the board of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 151(d) the holder of the preferred or special stock is entitled to the stated rights on dissolution or distribution of assets` `the stock is preferred or special stock of a class or series` `where the rights on dissolution or distribution are stated` `the certificate of incorporation expressly vests the authority in the board of directors` MEANS
        `the stock is preferred or special stock of a class or series`
    AND `s 151(a) the terms are stated where that subsection allows` `where the rights on dissolution or distribution are stated` `the certificate of incorporation expressly vests the authority in the board of directors`

-- Section 151(e): stock of a class or series may be made convertible into, or exchangeable for, shares of another class or series of the corporation's stock,
-- at the option of the holder or the corporation or on a specified event, at the price or rate and with the adjustments stated.
-- src:475 | Any stock of any class or of any series thereof may be made convertible into, or exchangeable for, at the option of either the holder or the corporation or upon the happening of a specified event, shares of any other class or classes or any other series of the same or any other class or classes of stock of the corporation, at such price or prices or at such rate or rates of exchange and with such adjustments as shall be stated in the certificate of incorporation or in the resolution or resolutions providing for the issue of such stock adopted by the board of directors as hereinabove provided.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 151(e) (src:475)
GIVEN `the shares to be received are shares of another class or series of the stock of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `where the conversion or exchange terms are stated` IS A `Where a provision is made`
      `the certificate of incorporation expressly vests the authority in the board of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 151(e) the stock may be made convertible or exchangeable` `the shares to be received are shares of another class or series of the stock of the corporation` `where the conversion or exchange terms are stated` `the certificate of incorporation expressly vests the authority in the board of directors` MEANS
        `the shares to be received are shares of another class or series of the stock of the corporation`
    AND `s 151(a) the terms are stated where that subsection allows` `where the conversion or exchange terms are stated` `the certificate of incorporation expressly vests the authority in the board of directors`

-- Section 151(f), first sentence: a corporation authorised to issue more than 1 class, or more than 1 series, must set the rights out on its certificates in full or in summary,
-- or (except as section 202 otherwise provides) may instead state that it will furnish them without charge to each stockholder who asks.
-- src:476 | If any corporation shall be authorized to issue more than 1 class of stock or more than 1 series of any class, the powers, designations, preferences and relative, participating, optional, or other special rights of each class of stock or series thereof and the qualifications, limitations or restrictions of such preferences and/or rights shall be set forth in full or summarized on the face or back of the certificate which the corporation shall issue to represent such class or series of stock, provided that, except as otherwise provided in § 202 of this title, in lieu of the foregoing requirements, there may be set forth on the face or back of the certificate which the corporation shall issue to represent such class or series of stock, a statement that the corporation will furnish without charge to each stockholder who so requests the powers, designations, preferences and relative, participating, optional, or other special rights of each class of stock or series thereof and the qualifications, limitations or restrictions of such preferences and/or rights. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 151(f) (src:476)
DECLARE `s 151(f) What a certificate says about class rights` HAS
    `the corporation is authorised to issue more than 1 class of stock or more than 1 series of any class` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate sets the rights out in full or summarises them`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate states that the corporation will furnish them without charge to each stockholder who so requests` IS A BOOLEAN
    `section 202 provides otherwise for the matter`                                                          IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 151(f) (src:476)
GIVEN c IS A `s 151(f) What a certificate says about class rights`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 151(f) the certificate states the rights as that subsection requires` c MEANS
        (NOT c's `the corporation is authorised to issue more than 1 class of stock or more than 1 series of any class`)
    OR  c's `the certificate sets the rights out in full or summarises them`
    OR  (    c's `the certificate states that the corporation will furnish them without charge to each stockholder who so requests`
         AND (NOT c's `section 202 provides otherwise for the matter`))

-- Section 151(f), second sentence: within a reasonable time after the issuance or transfer of uncertificated stock, the registered owner must be given a notice,
-- in writing or by electronic transmission, with the information that certificates must carry, or for section 151 a statement that the corporation will furnish it on request.
-- src:476 | Within a reasonable time after the issuance or transfer of uncertificated stock, the registered owner thereof shall be given a notice, in writing or by electronic transmission, containing the information required to be set forth or stated on certificates pursuant to this section or § 156, § 202(a), § 218(a) or § 364 of this title or with respect to this section a statement that the corporation will furnish without charge to each stockholder who so requests the powers, designations, preferences and relative participating, optional or other special rights of each class of stock or series thereof and the qualifications, limitations or restrictions of such preferences and/or rights. Except as otherwise expressly provided by law, the rights and obligations of the holders of uncertificated stock and the rights and obligations of the holders of certificates representing stock of the same class and series shall be identical.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 151(f) (src:476)
DECLARE `s 151(f) The notice to the registered owner of uncertificated stock` HAS
    `the notice was given in writing or by electronic transmission`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    -- a judgment: whether the time was "reasonable" is not decided here
    `the notice was given within a reasonable time after the issuance or transfer`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    -- out of range: the information that certificates must carry under sections 156 and 202(a) (this piece), 218(a) (dg4) and 364 (dg10), taken as stated
    `the notice contains the information required to be set forth or stated on certificates by section 156, 202(a), 218(a) or 364` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice contains the information required by section 151 or a statement that the corporation will furnish it without charge to each stockholder who so requests` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 151(f) (src:476)
GIVEN n IS A `s 151(f) The notice to the registered owner of uncertificated stock`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 151(f) the notice to the registered owner of uncertificated stock is as that subsection requires` n MEANS
        n's `the notice was given in writing or by electronic transmission`
    AND n's `the notice was given within a reasonable time after the issuance or transfer`
    AND n's `the notice contains the information required to be set forth or stated on certificates by section 156, 202(a), 218(a) or 364`
    AND n's `the notice contains the information required by section 151 or a statement that the corporation will furnish it without charge to each stockholder who so requests`

-- Section 151(f), last sentence: except as the law expressly provides otherwise, the holders of uncertificated stock and the holders of certificates of the same class and series have identical rights and obligations.
-- src:476 | Except as otherwise expressly provided by law, the rights and obligations of the holders of uncertificated stock and the rights and obligations of the holders of certificates representing stock of the same class and series shall be identical.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 151(f) (src:476)
GIVEN `the law expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 151(f) the holders of uncertificated stock and of certificates of the same class and series have identical rights and obligations` `the law expressly provides otherwise` MEANS
    NOT `the law expressly provides otherwise`

-- Section 151(g), first sentence: where the terms of a class or series are not in the certificate or an amendment but in a board resolution adopted under authority expressly vested
-- in the board by the certificate, a certificate of designations (the resolution and the number of shares) must be executed, acknowledged, filed and become effective under section 103.
-- src:477 | When any corporation desires to issue any shares of stock of any class or of any series of any class of which the powers, designations, preferences and relative, participating, optional or other rights, if any, or the qualifications, limitations or restrictions thereof, if any, shall not have been set forth in the certificate of incorporation or in any amendment thereto but shall be provided for in a resolution or resolutions adopted by the board of directors pursuant to authority expressly vested in it by the certificate of incorporation or any amendment thereto, a certificate of designations setting forth a copy of such resolution or resolutions and the number of shares of stock of such class or series as to which the resolution or resolutions apply shall be executed, acknowledged, filed and shall become effective, in accordance with § 103 of this title. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 151(g) (src:477)
GIVEN `the terms are provided for in a resolution adopted by the board under authority expressly vested in it by the certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms are set forth in the certificate of incorporation or an amendment to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 151(g) a certificate of designations is required` `the terms are provided for in a resolution adopted by the board under authority expressly vested in it by the certificate of incorporation` `the terms are set forth in the certificate of incorporation or an amendment to it` MEANS
        `the terms are provided for in a resolution adopted by the board under authority expressly vested in it by the certificate of incorporation`
    AND (NOT `the terms are set forth in the certificate of incorporation or an amendment to it`)

@ref 8 Del. C. § 151(g) (src:477)
GIVEN `a certificate of designations is required` IS A BOOLEAN
      -- out of range: section 103 (piece dg1): executed, acknowledged, filed and effective
      `the certificate of designations was executed, acknowledged and filed and has become effective in accordance with section 103` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 151(g) the requirement of a certificate of designations is met` `a certificate of designations is required` `the certificate of designations was executed, acknowledged and filed and has become effective in accordance with section 103` MEANS
        (NOT `a certificate of designations is required`)
    OR  `the certificate of designations was executed, acknowledged and filed and has become effective in accordance with section 103`

-- Section 151(g), second and third sentences: unless the resolution otherwise provides, the number of shares of the series may be increased (not above the authorised total of the class)
-- or decreased (not below the number then outstanding) by a certificate stating that the change was authorised by a board resolution. If the resolution otherwise provides, the text does not say: NOTHING.
-- src:477 | Unless otherwise provided in any such resolution or resolutions, the number of shares of stock of any such series to which such resolution or resolutions apply may be increased (but not above the total number of authorized shares of the class) or decreased (but not below the number of shares thereof then outstanding) by a certificate likewise executed, acknowledged and filed setting forth a statement that a specified increase or decrease therein had been authorized and directed by a resolution or resolutions likewise adopted by the board of directors. In case the number of such shares shall be decreased the number of shares so specified in the certificate shall resume the status which they had prior to the adoption of the first resolution or resolutions. When no shares of any such class or series are outstanding, either because none were issued or because no issued shares of any such class or series remain outstanding, a certificate setting forth a resolution or resolutions adopted by the board of directors that none of the authorized shares of such class or series are outstanding, and that none will be issued subject to the certificate of designations previously filed with respect to such class or series, may be executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with § 103 of this title and, when such certificate becomes effective, it shall have the effect of eliminating from the certificate of incorporation all matters set forth in the certificate of designations with respect to such class or series of stock. Unless otherwise provided in the certificate of incorporation, if no shares of stock have been issued of a class or series of stock established by a resolution of the board of directors, the voting powers, designations, preferences and relative, participating, optional or other rights, if any, or the qualifications, limitations or restrictions thereof, may be amended by a resolution or resolutions adopted by the board of directors. A certificate which:
-- src:477 | In case the number of such shares shall be decreased the number of shares so specified in the certificate shall resume the status which they had prior to the adoption of the first resolution or resolutions. When no shares of any such class or series are outstanding, either because none were issued or because no issued shares of any such class or series remain outstanding, a certificate setting forth a resolution or resolutions adopted by the board of directors that none of the authorized shares of such class or series are outstanding, and that none will be issued subject to the certificate of designations previously filed with respect to such class or series, may be executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with § 103 of this title and, when such certificate becomes effective, it shall have the effect of eliminating from the certificate of incorporation all matters set forth in the certificate of designations with respect to such class or series of stock. Unless otherwise provided in the certificate of incorporation, if no shares of stock have been issued of a class or series of stock established by a resolution of the board of directors, the voting powers, designations, preferences and relative, participating, optional or other rights, if any, or the qualifications, limitations or restrictions thereof, may be amended by a resolution or resolutions adopted by the board of directors. A certificate which:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 151(g) (src:477)
GIVEN `the resolution otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of shares of the series now` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of shares of the series after the change` IS A NUMBER
      `the total number of authorised shares of the class` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of shares of the series then outstanding` IS A NUMBER
      `a certificate stating that the change was authorised by a resolution of the board has been executed, acknowledged and filed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 151(g) the number of shares of the series may be changed` `the resolution otherwise provides` `the number of shares of the series now` `the number of shares of the series after the change` `the total number of authorised shares of the class` `the number of shares of the series then outstanding` `a certificate stating that the change was authorised by a resolution of the board has been executed, acknowledged and filed` MEANS
    IF `the resolution otherwise provides`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (    `a certificate stating that the change was authorised by a resolution of the board has been executed, acknowledged and filed`
               AND (    (`the number of shares of the series after the change` AT MOST `the number of shares of the series now`)
                    OR  (`the number of shares of the series after the change` AT MOST `the total number of authorised shares of the class`))
               AND (    (`the number of shares of the series after the change` AT LEAST `the number of shares of the series now`)
                    OR  (`the number of shares of the series after the change` AT LEAST `the number of shares of the series then outstanding`)))

-- When the number of shares is decreased, the shares so specified in the certificate resume the status they had before the first resolution.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 151(g) (src:477)
GIVEN `the number of shares of the series now` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of shares of the series after the change` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 151(g) the number of shares that resume the status they had before the first resolution` `the number of shares of the series now` `the number of shares of the series after the change` MEANS
    IF `the number of shares of the series after the change` LESS THAN `the number of shares of the series now`
    THEN `the number of shares of the series now` MINUS `the number of shares of the series after the change`
    ELSE 0

-- When no shares of the class or series are outstanding (none issued, or none remaining), a certificate setting out a board resolution that none are outstanding and none will be issued
-- under the certificate of designations may be filed under section 103 and, when effective, eliminates from the certificate of incorporation all matters in the certificate of designations.
-- src:477 | When no shares of any such class or series are outstanding, either because none were issued or because no issued shares of any such class or series remain outstanding, a certificate setting forth a resolution or resolutions adopted by the board of directors that none of the authorized shares of such class or series are outstanding, and that none will be issued subject to the certificate of designations previously filed with respect to such class or series, may be executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with § 103 of this title and, when such certificate becomes effective, it shall have the effect of eliminating from the certificate of incorporation all matters set forth in the certificate of designations with respect to such class or series of stock. Unless otherwise provided in the certificate of incorporation, if no shares of stock have been issued of a class or series of stock established by a resolution of the board of directors, the voting powers, designations, preferences and relative, participating, optional or other rights, if any, or the qualifications, limitations or restrictions thereof, may be amended by a resolution or resolutions adopted by the board of directors. A certificate which:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 151(g) (src:477)
GIVEN `no shares of the class or series are outstanding, either because none were issued or because none remain outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the board adopted a resolution that none of the authorised shares are outstanding and that none will be issued subject to the certificate of designations previously filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      -- out of range: section 103 (piece dg1)
      `the certificate setting forth the resolution has been executed, acknowledged and filed and has become effective in accordance with section 103` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 151(g) the certificate eliminates from the certificate of incorporation the matters in the certificate of designations` `no shares of the class or series are outstanding, either because none were issued or because none remain outstanding` `the board adopted a resolution that none of the authorised shares are outstanding and that none will be issued subject to the certificate of designations previously filed` `the certificate setting forth the resolution has been executed, acknowledged and filed and has become effective in accordance with section 103` MEANS
        `no shares of the class or series are outstanding, either because none were issued or because none remain outstanding`
    AND `the board adopted a resolution that none of the authorised shares are outstanding and that none will be issued subject to the certificate of designations previously filed`
    AND `the certificate setting forth the resolution has been executed, acknowledged and filed and has become effective in accordance with section 103`

-- Unless the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise, if no shares have been issued of a class or series established by a board resolution,
-- the board may amend its voting powers, designations, preferences and rights by a resolution.
