§ `Section 152: issuance of stock; lawful consideration; fully paid stock`

-- Section 152(a): the board decides the form and manner of payment, and may authorise issue for cash, any tangible or intangible property or any benefit to the corporation, or any combination,
-- in the numbers, at the times and for the consideration set forth in a resolution of the board.
-- src:485 | The consideration for subscriptions to, or the purchase of, the capital stock to be issued by a corporation shall be paid in the form and in the manner that the board of directors shall determine. The board of directors may authorize capital stock to be issued for consideration consisting of cash, any tangible or intangible property or any benefit to the corporation, or any combination thereof. Stock may be issued in 1 or more transactions, in the numbers, at the times and for the consideration as set forth in a resolution of the board of directors.
-- src:485 | The board of directors may authorize capital stock to be issued for consideration consisting of cash, any tangible or intangible property or any benefit to the corporation, or any combination thereof. Stock may be issued in 1 or more transactions, in the numbers, at the times and for the consideration as set forth in a resolution of the board of directors.
-- src:485 | Stock may be issued in 1 or more transactions, in the numbers, at the times and for the consideration as set forth in a resolution of the board of directors.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 152(a) (src:485)
DECLARE `s 152(a) The consideration for an issue of stock` HAS
    `it consists of cash`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `it consists of tangible property`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `it consists of intangible property`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `it consists of a benefit to the corporation`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the numbers, times and consideration are set forth in a resolution of the board of directors` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 152(a) (src:485)
GIVEN c IS A `s 152(a) The consideration for an issue of stock`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 152(a) the board has authorised the issue of stock for the consideration` c MEANS
        (    c's `it consists of cash`
         OR  c's `it consists of tangible property`
         OR  c's `it consists of intangible property`
         OR  c's `it consists of a benefit to the corporation`)
    AND c's `the numbers, times and consideration are set forth in a resolution of the board of directors`

-- Section 152(b): a board resolution may delegate to a person or body, in addition to the board, the authority to enter into 1 or more transactions to issue stock,
-- provided the resolution fixes (i) a maximum number of shares, (ii) a time period during which they may be issued and (iii) the minimum consideration;
-- and no such resolution shall permit a person or body to issue stock to itself.
-- src:486 | A resolution of the board of directors may delegate to a person or body, in addition to the board of directors, the authority to enter into 1 or more transactions to issue stock, and with respect to such transactions, shares of stock may be issued in the numbers, at the times and for the consideration as such person or body may determine; provided the resolution fixes (i) a maximum number of shares that may be issued pursuant to such resolution, (ii) a time period during which such shares may be issued and (iii) the minimum consideration for which such shares may be issued. No such resolution shall permit a person or body to issue stock to such person or body.
-- src:486 | No such resolution shall permit a person or body to issue stock to such person or body.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 152(b) (src:486)
GIVEN `the resolution fixes a maximum number of shares that may be issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution fixes a time period during which the shares may be issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution fixes the minimum consideration for which the shares may be issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution permits the person or body to issue stock to itself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 152(b) the resolution validly delegates the authority to issue stock` `the resolution fixes a maximum number of shares that may be issued` `the resolution fixes a time period during which the shares may be issued` `the resolution fixes the minimum consideration for which the shares may be issued` `the resolution permits the person or body to issue stock to itself` MEANS
        `the resolution fixes a maximum number of shares that may be issued`
    AND `the resolution fixes a time period during which the shares may be issued`
    AND `the resolution fixes the minimum consideration for which the shares may be issued`
    AND (NOT `the resolution permits the person or body to issue stock to itself`)

-- The three limits a delegating resolution fixes, and one issue made under it.
-- The text does not say whether the minimum consideration is per share or for the whole issue; both figures below are in the resolution's own unit (Fork F2).
