GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 153(c) the treasury shares may be disposed of in that manner` `the treasury shares are disposed of in the same manner that shares are issued under section 152(a) to (d)` `the stockholders determined the consideration` `the certificate of incorporation provides that the stockholders determine the consideration` `the consideration consists of cash, tangible or intangible property or a benefit to the corporation, or a combination` MEANS
        `the consideration consists of cash, tangible or intangible property or a benefit to the corporation, or a combination`
    AND (    `the treasury shares are disposed of in the same manner that shares are issued under section 152(a) to (d)`
         OR  (    `the stockholders determined the consideration`
              AND `the certificate of incorporation provides that the stockholders determine the consideration`))

-- Section 153(d): if the certificate reserves to the stockholders the right to determine the consideration, they do so by a vote of a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote,
-- unless the certificate requires a greater vote. A greater vote that is not in fact greater leaves the majority in force (the answer needs both; a requirement of p% is met by at least p%: Fork F21).
-- src:496 | If the certificate of incorporation reserves to the stockholders the right to determine the consideration for the issue of any shares, the stockholders shall, unless the certificate requires a greater vote, do so by a vote of a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote thereon.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 153(d) (src:496)
GIVEN `the greater vote the certificate of incorporation requires, if any` IS A MAYBE `Vote requirement`
      `the votes in favor` IS A NUMBER
      `the outstanding stock entitled to vote, in votes` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 153(d) the stockholders' determination of the consideration is adopted` `the greater vote the certificate of incorporation requires, if any` `the votes in favor` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote, in votes` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the greater vote the certificate of incorporation requires, if any`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote`) `the votes in favor` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote, in votes`
    WHEN JUST greater THEN
        CONSIDER `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote`) `the votes in favor` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote, in votes`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST m THEN
            CONSIDER `the vote carries` greater `the votes in favor` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote, in votes`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST g THEN JUST (m AND g)

§ `Section 155: fractions of shares`

-- A corporation may, but need not, issue fractions of a share. If it does not, it shall (1) arrange for the disposition of fractional interests by those entitled,
-- (2) pay in cash the fair value of fractions as of the time those entitled to them are determined, or (3) issue scrip or warrants in registered form that entitle the holder to a full share on surrender of an aggregate full share.
-- "Fair value" is paid in full when the amount paid is at least the fair value (Fork F15).
-- src:504 | A corporation may, but shall not be required to, issue fractions of a share. If it does not issue fractions of a share, it shall (1) arrange for the disposition of fractional interests by those entitled thereto, (2) pay in cash the fair value of fractions of a share as of the time when those entitled to receive such fractions are determined or (3) issue scrip or warrants in registered form (either represented by a certificate or uncertificated) which shall entitle the holder to receive a full share upon the surrender of such scrip or warrants aggregating a full share. A certificate for a fractional share or an uncertificated fractional share shall, but scrip or warrants shall not unless otherwise provided therein, entitle the holder to exercise voting rights, to receive dividends thereon and to participate in any of the assets of the corporation in the event of liquidation. The board of directors may cause scrip or warrants to be issued subject to the conditions that they shall become void if not exchanged for certificates representing the full shares or uncertificated full shares before a specified date, or subject to the conditions that the shares for which scrip or warrants are exchangeable may be sold by the corporation and the proceeds thereof distributed to the holders of scrip or warrants, or subject to any other conditions which the board of directors may impose.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 155 (src:504)
GIVEN `the corporation issues fractions of a share` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation arranged for the disposition of fractional interests by those entitled thereto` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of cash the corporation paid for the fractions` IS A NUMBER
      `the fair value of the fractions as of the time when those entitled to receive them were determined` IS A NUMBER
      `the corporation issued scrip or warrants in registered form that entitle the holder to a full share on surrender of scrip or warrants aggregating a full share` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 155 the corporation has dealt with fractional interests as the section requires` `the corporation issues fractions of a share` `the corporation arranged for the disposition of fractional interests by those entitled thereto` `the amount of cash the corporation paid for the fractions` `the fair value of the fractions as of the time when those entitled to receive them were determined` `the corporation issued scrip or warrants in registered form that entitle the holder to a full share on surrender of scrip or warrants aggregating a full share` MEANS
        `the corporation issues fractions of a share`
    OR  `the corporation arranged for the disposition of fractional interests by those entitled thereto`
    OR  (`the amount of cash the corporation paid for the fractions` AT LEAST `the fair value of the fractions as of the time when those entitled to receive them were determined`)
    OR  `the corporation issued scrip or warrants in registered form that entitle the holder to a full share on surrender of scrip or warrants aggregating a full share`

-- What the holder of a fractional interest holds, and the three rights a fractional share carries.
-- src:504 | A certificate for a fractional share or an uncertificated fractional share shall, but scrip or warrants shall not unless otherwise provided therein, entitle the holder to exercise voting rights, to receive dividends thereon and to participate in any of the assets of the corporation in the event of liquidation. The board of directors may cause scrip or warrants to be issued subject to the conditions that they shall become void if not exchanged for certificates representing the full shares or uncertificated full shares before a specified date, or subject to the conditions that the shares for which scrip or warrants are exchangeable may be sold by the corporation and the proceeds thereof distributed to the holders of scrip or warrants, or subject to any other conditions which the board of directors may impose.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 155 (src:504)
DECLARE `s 155 What the holder of a fractional interest holds` IS ONE OF
    `a certificate for a fractional share under s 155`
    `an uncertificated fractional share under s 155`
    `scrip or warrants under s 155`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 155 (src:504)
DECLARE `s 155 A right a fractional interest may carry` IS ONE OF
    `the right to exercise voting rights under s 155`
    `the right to receive dividends under s 155`
    `the right to participate in the assets of the corporation in the event of liquidation under s 155`

-- A certificate for a fractional share or an uncertificated fractional share entitles the holder to vote, to receive dividends and to participate in the assets on liquidation;
-- scrip or warrants do not, unless they so provide.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 155 (src:504)
GIVEN `what the holder holds` IS A `s 155 What the holder of a fractional interest holds`
      `the right` IS A `s 155 A right a fractional interest may carry`
      `the scrip or warrants provide that they carry the right` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 155 the holder of the fractional interest is entitled to the right` `what the holder holds` `the right` `the scrip or warrants provide that they carry the right` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what the holder holds`
    WHEN `a certificate for a fractional share under s 155` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an uncertificated fractional share under s 155` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `scrip or warrants under s 155` THEN `the scrip or warrants provide that they carry the right`

-- The board may cause scrip or warrants to be issued on conditions: that they become void if not exchanged for certificates or uncertificated full shares before a specified date,
-- that the shares for which they are exchangeable may be sold and the proceeds distributed, or any other condition the board imposes.
-- "Before a specified date" is read literally: exchange on the specified date itself is too late (Fork F4).
-- src:504 | The board of directors may cause scrip or warrants to be issued subject to the conditions that they shall become void if not exchanged for certificates representing the full shares or uncertificated full shares before a specified date, or subject to the conditions that the shares for which scrip or warrants are exchangeable may be sold by the corporation and the proceeds thereof distributed to the holders of scrip or warrants, or subject to any other conditions which the board of directors may impose.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 155 (src:504)
GIVEN `the scrip or warrants carry a condition that they become void if not exchanged for full shares before a specified date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the scrip or warrants were exchanged for full shares, if they were` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the specified date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 155 the scrip or warrants have become void` `the scrip or warrants carry a condition that they become void if not exchanged for full shares before a specified date` `the day the scrip or warrants were exchanged for full shares, if they were` `the specified date` MEANS
        `the scrip or warrants carry a condition that they become void if not exchanged for full shares before a specified date`
    AND (    CONSIDER `the day the scrip or warrants were exchanged for full shares, if they were`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
             WHEN JUST exchanged THEN (exchanged AT LEAST `the specified date`))

-- The board may cause scrip or warrants to be issued subject to any of three kinds of condition: that they become void if not exchanged before a specified date;
-- that the shares for which they are exchangeable may be sold and the proceeds distributed to the holders; or any other condition the board may impose.
-- The text sets no limit on the third kind, so the board may attach any condition, but only to scrip or warrants issued in registered form in lieu of fractions under (3).
-- src:504 | or subject to the conditions that the shares for which scrip or warrants are exchangeable may be sold by the corporation and the proceeds thereof distributed to the holders of scrip or warrants, or subject to any other conditions which the board of directors may impose.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 155 (src:504)
DECLARE `s 155 A condition on which scrip or warrants may be issued` IS ONE OF
    `that they become void if not exchanged for full shares before a specified date under s 155`
    `that the shares for which they are exchangeable may be sold and the proceeds distributed to the holders under s 155`
    `any other condition which the board of directors may impose under s 155`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 155 (src:504)
GIVEN `the corporation issues scrip or warrants in registered form in lieu of fractions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition` IS A `s 155 A condition on which scrip or warrants may be issued`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 155 the board may cause scrip or warrants to be issued subject to the condition` `the corporation issues scrip or warrants in registered form in lieu of fractions` `the condition` MEANS
        `the corporation issues scrip or warrants in registered form in lieu of fractions`
    AND (    CONSIDER `the condition`
             WHEN `that they become void if not exchanged for full shares before a specified date under s 155` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `that the shares for which they are exchangeable may be sold and the proceeds distributed to the holders under s 155` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `any other condition which the board of directors may impose under s 155` THEN TRUE)

§ `Section 156: partly paid shares`

-- A corporation may issue the whole or any part of its shares as partly paid and subject to call for the remainder of the consideration.
-- On the face or back of each certificate for such shares, or on the books and records for uncertificated ones, the total consideration and the amount paid must be stated.
-- src:508 | Any corporation may issue the whole or any part of its shares as partly paid and subject to call for the remainder of the consideration to be paid therefor. Upon the face or back of each stock certificate issued to represent any such partly paid shares, or upon the books and records of the corporation in the case of uncertificated partly paid shares, the total amount of the consideration to be paid therefor and the amount paid thereon shall be stated. Upon the declaration of any dividend on fully paid shares, the corporation shall declare a dividend upon partly paid shares of the same class, but only upon the basis of the percentage of the consideration actually paid thereon.
-- src:508 | Upon the face or back of each stock certificate issued to represent any such partly paid shares, or upon the books and records of the corporation in the case of uncertificated partly paid shares, the total amount of the consideration to be paid therefor and the amount paid thereon shall be stated. Upon the declaration of any dividend on fully paid shares, the corporation shall declare a dividend upon partly paid shares of the same class, but only upon the basis of the percentage of the consideration actually paid thereon.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 156 (src:508)
GIVEN `the partly paid shares are represented by a certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the face or back of the certificate states the total consideration to be paid and the amount paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the books and records of the corporation state the total consideration to be paid and the amount paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 156 the total consideration and the amount paid are stated as the section requires` `the partly paid shares are represented by a certificate` `the face or back of the certificate states the total consideration to be paid and the amount paid` `the books and records of the corporation state the total consideration to be paid and the amount paid` MEANS
    IF `the partly paid shares are represented by a certificate`
    THEN `the face or back of the certificate states the total consideration to be paid and the amount paid`
    ELSE `the books and records of the corporation state the total consideration to be paid and the amount paid`

-- On declaring a dividend on fully paid shares the corporation shall declare a dividend on partly paid shares of the same class, but only on the basis of the percentage of the consideration actually paid.
-- NOTHING when the figures cannot be a payment: a total consideration of 0 or less, or an amount paid below 0 or above the total.
-- src:508 | Upon the declaration of any dividend on fully paid shares, the corporation shall declare a dividend upon partly paid shares of the same class, but only upon the basis of the percentage of the consideration actually paid thereon.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 156 (src:508)
GIVEN `the dividend declared on each fully paid share` IS A NUMBER
      `the total consideration to be paid for each partly paid share` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount paid on each partly paid share` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 156 the dividend on each partly paid share` `the dividend declared on each fully paid share` `the total consideration to be paid for each partly paid share` `the amount paid on each partly paid share` MEANS
    IF     (`the total consideration to be paid for each partly paid share` GREATER THAN 0)
       AND (`the amount paid on each partly paid share` AT LEAST 0)
       AND (`the amount paid on each partly paid share` AT MOST `the total consideration to be paid for each partly paid share`)
    THEN JUST (`the dividend declared on each fully paid share` TIMES (`the amount paid on each partly paid share` DIVIDED BY `the total consideration to be paid for each partly paid share`))
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 157: rights and options respecting stock`

-- Section 157(a): subject to any provisions in the certificate of incorporation, a corporation may create and issue rights or options entitling the holders to acquire its capital stock.
-- src:512 | Subject to any provisions in the certificate of incorporation, every corporation may create and issue, whether or not in connection with the issue and sale of any shares of stock or other securities of the corporation, rights or options entitling the holders thereof to acquire from the corporation any shares of its capital stock of any class or classes of the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 157(a) (src:512)
GIVEN `a provision of the certificate of incorporation forbids the creation or issue of the rights or options` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 157(a) the corporation may create and issue the rights or options` `a provision of the certificate of incorporation forbids the creation or issue of the rights or options` MEANS
    NOT `a provision of the certificate of incorporation forbids the creation or issue of the rights or options`

-- Section 157(b): rights and options may be issued in the numbers, at the times and for the consideration set forth in a board resolution;
-- the terms on which shares may be acquired on exercise shall be as stated in the certificate or in a board resolution.
-- src:513 | Rights and options may be issued in 1 or more transactions, in the numbers, at the times and for the consideration as set forth in a resolution of the board of directors. The terms upon which, including the time or times which may be limited or unlimited in duration, at or within which, and the consideration for which any such shares may be acquired from the corporation upon the exercise of any such right or option, shall be as stated in the certificate of incorporation, or in a resolution of the board of directors.
-- src:513 | The terms upon which, including the time or times which may be limited or unlimited in duration, at or within which, and the consideration for which any such shares may be acquired from the corporation upon the exercise of any such right or option, shall be as stated in the certificate of incorporation, or in a resolution of the board of directors.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 157(b) (src:513)
GIVEN `the numbers, times and consideration of the rights or options are set forth in a resolution of the board of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `where the terms of exercise are stated` IS A `Where a provision is made`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 157(b) the rights or options are issued and their terms stated as that subsection requires` `the numbers, times and consideration of the rights or options are set forth in a resolution of the board of directors` `where the terms of exercise are stated` MEANS
        `the numbers, times and consideration of the rights or options are set forth in a resolution of the board of directors`
    AND (    `where the terms of exercise are stated` EQUALS `in the certificate of incorporation`
         OR  `where the terms of exercise are stated` EQUALS `in a resolution of the board of directors`)

-- Section 157(c): a board resolution may delegate to a person or body the authority to issue rights or options, provided it fixes (i) the maximum number of shares issuable on exercise,
-- (ii) a time period for issuing the rights or options and a time period for issuing the shares on exercise, and (iii) the minimum consideration (if any) for the rights or options and for the shares on exercise;
-- and no such resolution shall permit a person or body to issue rights or options to itself.
-- src:514 | The board of directors may adopt a resolution to delegate to a person or body, in addition to the board of directors, the authority to enter into 1 or more transactions to issue rights or options, and with respect to such transactions, the rights or options may be issued in such numbers, at such times and for such consideration, and the terms upon which shares may be acquired from the corporation upon the exercise of any such rights or options may be, as such person or body may determine; provided that the resolution fixes (i) the maximum number of shares issuable upon exercise of the rights or options that may be issued pursuant to such resolution, (ii) a time period during which such rights or options, and a time period during which the shares issuable upon exercise thereof, may be issued, and (iii) the minimum consideration (if any) for which such rights or options may be issued and the minimum consideration for the shares issuable upon exercise thereof. No such resolution shall permit a person or body to issue rights or options to such person or body.
-- src:514 | No such resolution shall permit a person or body to issue rights or options to such person or body.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 157(c) (src:514)
GIVEN `the resolution fixes the maximum number of shares issuable upon exercise of the rights or options` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution fixes a time period for issuing the rights or options and a time period for issuing the shares issuable on exercise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution fixes the minimum consideration, if any, for the rights or options and for the shares issuable on exercise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution permits the person or body to issue rights or options to itself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 157(c) the resolution validly delegates the authority to issue rights or options` `the resolution fixes the maximum number of shares issuable upon exercise of the rights or options` `the resolution fixes a time period for issuing the rights or options and a time period for issuing the shares issuable on exercise` `the resolution fixes the minimum consideration, if any, for the rights or options and for the shares issuable on exercise` `the resolution permits the person or body to issue rights or options to itself` MEANS
        `the resolution fixes the maximum number of shares issuable upon exercise of the rights or options`
    AND `the resolution fixes a time period for issuing the rights or options and a time period for issuing the shares issuable on exercise`
    AND `the resolution fixes the minimum consideration, if any, for the rights or options and for the shares issuable on exercise`
    AND (NOT `the resolution permits the person or body to issue rights or options to itself`)

-- The limits a delegating resolution fixes under section 157(c), and one issue of rights or options made under it.
-- As in section 152(b), the text does not say whether a minimum consideration is per right or for the whole issue (Fork F2).
-- src:514 | the rights or options may be issued in such numbers, at such times and for such consideration, and the terms upon which shares may be acquired from the corporation upon the exercise of any such rights or options may be, as such person or body may determine; provided that the resolution fixes (i) the maximum number of shares issuable upon exercise of the rights or options that may be issued pursuant to such resolution, (ii) a time period during which such rights or options, and a time period during which the shares issuable upon exercise thereof, may be issued, and (iii) the minimum consideration (if any) for which such rights or options may be issued and the minimum consideration for the shares issuable upon exercise thereof. No such resolution shall permit a person or body to issue rights or options to such person or body.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 157(c) (src:514)
DECLARE `s 157(c) A delegating resolution` HAS
    `the maximum number of shares issuable upon exercise`            IS A NUMBER
    `the first day for issuing the rights or options`                 IS A DATE
    `the last day for issuing the rights or options`                  IS A DATE
    `the first day for issuing the shares on exercise`                IS A DATE
    `the last day for issuing the shares on exercise`                 IS A DATE
    `the minimum consideration for the rights or options, if any`     IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the minimum consideration for the shares on exercise`            IS A NUMBER

@ref 8 Del. C. § 157(c) (src:514)
DECLARE `s 157(c) One issue of rights or options under a delegating resolution` HAS
    `the number of shares issuable upon exercise of those already issued` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of shares issuable upon exercise of this issue`           IS A NUMBER
    `the day the rights or options are issued`                            IS A DATE
    `the day the shares are to be issued on exercise`                     IS A DATE
    `the consideration for the rights or options`                         IS A NUMBER
    `the consideration for the shares on exercise`                        IS A NUMBER
    `the rights or options are issued to the person or body that issues them` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 157(c) (src:514)
GIVEN r IS A `s 157(c) A delegating resolution`
      i IS A `s 157(c) One issue of rights or options under a delegating resolution`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 157(c) the issue of rights or options is within the delegating resolution` r i MEANS
        ((i's `the number of shares issuable upon exercise of those already issued`) PLUS (i's `the number of shares issuable upon exercise of this issue`)) AT MOST (r's `the maximum number of shares issuable upon exercise`)
    AND (i's `the day the rights or options are issued`) AT LEAST (r's `the first day for issuing the rights or options`)
    AND (i's `the day the rights or options are issued`) AT MOST (r's `the last day for issuing the rights or options`)
    AND (i's `the day the shares are to be issued on exercise`) AT LEAST (r's `the first day for issuing the shares on exercise`)
    AND (i's `the day the shares are to be issued on exercise`) AT MOST (r's `the last day for issuing the shares on exercise`)
    AND (    CONSIDER r's `the minimum consideration for the rights or options, if any`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
             WHEN JUST least THEN ((i's `the consideration for the rights or options`) AT LEAST least))
    AND (i's `the consideration for the shares on exercise`) AT LEAST (r's `the minimum consideration for the shares on exercise`)
    AND (NOT i's `the rights or options are issued to the person or body that issues them`)

-- Section 157(d): a provision of a resolution under (b) or (c) may depend on facts ascertainable outside the resolution, if the resolution clearly and expressly sets forth how the facts operate;
-- "facts" includes the occurrence of any event, including a determination or action by any person or body, including the corporation;
-- and where the resolution delegates, the provisions under (c)(i) to (iii) may not depend on a determination or action by the delegate.
-- src:515 | Any provision in a resolution contemplated by subsection (b) or (c) of this section may be made dependent on facts ascertainable outside the resolution, provided the manner in which such facts shall operate upon the resolution is clearly and expressly set forth in such resolution. The term “facts,” as used in this section, includes, but is not limited to, the occurrence of any event, including a determination or action by any person or body, including the corporation; provided that, if the resolution delegates to a person or body the authority to enter into 1 or more transactions to issue rights or options pursuant to subsection (c) of this section, the provisions contemplated by paragraphs (c)(i) through (iii) of this section may not be made dependent on a determination or action by such person or body.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 157(d) (src:515)
GIVEN `the resolution is one contemplated by subsection (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a provision depends on facts ascertainable outside the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution clearly and expressly sets forth the manner in which the facts operate on the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 157(d) the provision may be made dependent on facts ascertainable outside the resolution` `the resolution is one contemplated by subsection (b) or (c)` `a provision depends on facts ascertainable outside the resolution` `the resolution clearly and expressly sets forth the manner in which the facts operate on the resolution` MEANS
        `the resolution is one contemplated by subsection (b) or (c)`
    AND (    (NOT `a provision depends on facts ascertainable outside the resolution`)
         OR  `the resolution clearly and expressly sets forth the manner in which the facts operate on the resolution`)

-- src:515 | The term “facts,” as used in this section, includes, but is not limited to, the occurrence of any event, including a determination or action by any person or body, including the corporation; provided that, if the resolution delegates to a person or body the authority to enter into 1 or more transactions to issue rights or options pursuant to subsection (c) of this section, the provisions contemplated by paragraphs (c)(i) through (iii) of this section may not be made dependent on a determination or action by such person or body.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 157(d) (src:515)
